# Project One Get-Item Pseudocode
#
# Graded checkpoint: Module Five Project One
# Later use: get-item and inventory design for M7 Project Two
#
# Review the course-provided get-item flowchart before completing this file.
# Write pseudocode, not Python code. Use clear indentation and course-appropriate
# keywords such as INPUT, OUTPUT, IF, ELSE, SET, ADD, or similar terms.

START get_item

   SET current_room as room the player is currently in
   SET room_item as the item that is in the current_room
   SET inventory as the items the player currently has
   PRINT "Type the item you wish to obtain:"
   GET item_command
   SET valid_item to FALSE
   IF item_command matches room_item
   Set valid item to TRUE
   ENDIF
   IF valid_item = TRUE
   ADD item_command to your inventory
   PUT "You picked up" + item_command + "."
   SET room_item = NONE
   ELSE
   PUT "There is no item by that name."
   ENDIF
   PUT "Here is your inventory" + inventory

    RETURN TO MAIN GAME LOOP.

END get_item